source are kept. This fork does not grant any trademark rights in the VoiceInk name.

Modified by the maintainer of https://github.com/qaws81877/sulsul (2026).

Changes in this fork include:
- Rebranded the app as 술술 (product name Sulsul) with its own bundle ID, data folder, and Keychain service so it does not share data with VoiceInk.
- Removed the license, trial, and purchase system, including Polar.
- Stopped contacting the original author's servers (announcements, Sparkle appcast, GitHub star prompt, and related links).
- Removed the VoiceInk Refine local model and its XPC service. That model's license does not allow redistribution.
- Turned off iCloud dictionary sync that depended on the original iCloud container.
- Onboarding can skip the transcription-model download or use a Whisper model instead of requiring Parakeet.

M2 additions:
- A fresh install defaults the transcription language to Korean (`ko`) and preselects the non-quantized Whisper model `ggml-large-v3-turbo`. Saved language and model choices are left alone.
- Regex filler-word removal is off unless the user turns it back on. The word list is still editable.
- The default cleanup prompt is the bundled Korean prompt (`prompt_ko_v3`). A new install sends it to OpenAI `gpt-6-luna`, then Anthropic `claude-haiku-5-5` if OpenAI fails, stalls, or no OpenAI key is saved. Other providers stay available when chosen by hand.
- Korean (`ko`) is an app language. English remains the development language, and the app follows the macOS language.
- API keys are stored in the local Keychain only. They are not iCloud-synced, and none are bundled.

Each person enters their own API keys. No API keys are bundled.

